## Design Patterns

Design patterns are tested solutions for common problems in software development.

## Singleton

Ensures only one instance of a class:

```php
class Database {
    private static ?Database $instance = null;

    private function __construct() {}

    public static function getInstance(): Database {
        if (self::$instance === null) {
            self::$instance = new self();
        }
        return self::$instance;
    }
}
```

## Factory

Creates objects without specifying exactly which class to use:

```php
class TransportFactory {
    public static function create(string $type): Transport {
        return match($type) {
            'car' => new Car(),
            'bike' => new Bike(),
            default => throw new Exception('Unknown type')
        };
    }
}
```

## Observer

Notifies multiple objects about state changes:

```php
interface Observer {
    public function update(Subject $subject);
}

class Subject {
    private array $observers = [];

    public function attach(Observer $observer): void {
        $this->observers[] = $observer;
    }

    public function notify(): void {
        foreach ($this->observers as $observer) {
            $observer->update($this);
        }
    }
}
```

## Conclusion

Mastering design patterns significantly improves your code quality.

